  "instructions": [
    "Season the chicken thighs with salt and pepper.",
    "Heat olive oil in a Dutch oven over medium heat and brown the chicken thighs on all sides.",
    "Remove the chicken and set aside.",
    "Sauté onion, garlic, and ginger in the same pot until fragrant.",
    "Add the spice blend and tomato paste, cooking for 2 minutes to bloom the flavors.",
    "Return the chicken to the pot and pour in chicken broth.",
    "Bring to a gentle simmer, cover, and cook for 30 minutes until the chicken is tender.",
    "Stir in fresh mint leaves and lemon juice, adjusting seasoning as needed.",
    "Serve hot over couscous or flatbread.",
    "Ensure poultry is cooked to an internal temperature of 74°C / 165°F (juices run clear, no pink remaining) before serving."
